  "proof": {
    "per_96_byte_group": "three contiguous YMM loads expose six 128-bit lanes; four of the eight 12-byte coefficient windows cross a 128-bit boundary.  Each desired output register pairs one crossing window with one non-crossing window at a different byte alignment, so a uniform lane-local shuffle cannot form both. The best packet-window factorization needs three source-lane gathers, two aligned crossing-window vectors, and four final lane merges per group.",
    "avx2_constraint": "vpshufb and vpalignr are independently lane-local; vpalignr applies one immediate to both 128-bit lanes"
  },
